        <body>
            <div xml:id="d215-a1">

                <pb facs="0177" n="157" sameAs="frus:frus1864p3/pg157"/>

                <head>Mr. Townsend to Mr.
                        Seward</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">War Department, Adjutant General’s
                                Office,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-10-04"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >October</hi> 4, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I am directed by the Secretary of War to
                    transmit to you the enclosed documents in relation to the arrival in Texas of a
                    Mexican force under Cortinas, with the request that after you have perused the
                    same, they may be returned to this office for file.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, sir, very respectfully, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>E. D. TOWNSEND, <hi rendition="#italic">Assistant Adjutant
                        General.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Secretary of State.</hi></p>
                </postscript>















